WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.140
We haven't talked about investing for a long time, so let's chat with everyone today.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:08.380
Many friends who are familiar with me know that I am a long-term investor in Tesla, and I have been holding it since the end of 2018.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:11.140
 this is the most successful investment of my life.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.660
Therefore, many old viewers have asked me, why don't you try to find the next Tesla?

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.919
For example,  people often ask me, why don't you invest in NVIDIA?

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.880
Seeing the recent crazy rise of companies like AMD and Oracle,

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.620
including Lemonade, which a good friend of mine invested in, is also growing like crazy.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.340
Many people will be curious, why would you miss these obvious investment opportunities,

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.360
and not invest in these hot stocks?

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.420
So, today I want to use this video to briefly share why I don't try to find the next Tesla,

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:41.840
or why I don't pursue investing in those so-called hot stocks.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:47.440
I will mainly talk about four reasons, and among them, I will also recommend a book to everyone.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.230
But before we start,

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.960
I want to take thirty seconds to thank the channel's long-term partner, Interactive Brokers. IB is

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.400
an award-winning and widely recognized global broker, and it is also my platform for investing in US stocks.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.500
I like it for two main reasons. First, its transaction costs are very low.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.500
In many regions, there are no handling fees or the fees are so low that they have no impact.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.980
Second, its currency exchange costs are very competitive.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.660
 I often have to convert Canadian dollars to US dollars when buying US stocks in Canada.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:14.560
Compared to Canadian brokers that charge a handling fee of more than 1.5%, IB's exchange rate is simply

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.360
too low, and that alone is enough for me to choose them.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.979
IB has many other advantages, far beyond what I have mentioned, such as paying interest on cash in eligible accounts.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:26.540
Its options trading function is also very powerful and inexpensive.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:30.400
I strongly recommend that you click the link in the comment section to check out Interactive Brokers.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.200
Clicking the link will benefit me, so it's a way of supporting me.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.280
Okay, let's get started.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.680
I don't look for the next Tesla because doing so is meaningless in most cases.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.280
It's a kind of half-measure.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.740
Those who often watch my videos know that I am a die-hard fan of the American drama,  Breaking Bad. You can tell from my T-shirt.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.560
There is an episode in Breaking Bad that left a particularly deep impression on me.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.760
It's called "No half measure."

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:59.560
This line comes from the character Mike in the show, and it means,  either don't do it, or do it all the way.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.020
This has always been one of my life mottos.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.400
In fact, this is even more true in investing.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.820
 in portfolio management, there are basically two major schools of thought.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.460
 the first is the complete diversification school.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:17.480
I have always recommended that ordinary people invest in S&amp;P 500 index funds.  this is an extremely diversified strategy.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:23.100
You can even configure a global index, own stocks of all companies, own everything.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.140
The second extreme is,  the complete concentration school,

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:31.320
which is to highly concentrate your investment portfolio in a very small number of stocks, or even just one or two.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:36.940
These two schools of thought actually correspond to two seemingly contradictory sayings in the investment world. One is,

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.540
 don't put all your eggs in one basket, and the other is,

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.360
 put all your eggs in one basket, and then carry that basket well.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.640
The former talks about diversification, while the latter talks about concentration.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.800
So which one is right?

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:54.620
I think both are right. They correspond to the optimal solutions under different conditions and goals.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:03:01.220
Let's talk about concentrated investing first. If you want to,  make big money in the stock market, you usually need two conditions:

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:06.300
enough principal, and an investment target that can multiply many times, for example, a ten-bagger stock.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:12.200
To achieve this, you must put all your eggs in one basket, which is an extremely risky behavior.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:17.140
Most people actually don't have the objective conditions to do so, because most people,

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:18.660
actually can't afford to lose.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:24.299
There are only two situations where you can bear this kind of risk. Either you bet your entire life savings,

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.940
win and change your life, lose and be doomed forever; or your assets are already so large

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:33.500
that you can take out a very considerable amount of principal for concentrated investment, and even if this investment fails,

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.000
your overall financial safety margin will remain stable.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.260
Obviously, very few people can meet these conditions.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.940
Now let's look at diversified investing. This path seems ordinary,

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.160
but for most people, it is a wise strategic choice.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:51.000
Because the real purpose of diversified investing is not just to diversify risks, but to concentrate attention.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.020
When you choose to buy the S&amp;P 500 index, you are actually making a decision.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:04:00.940
I give up my ambition to pursue excess returns in the stock market in exchange for my most precious resources, time and energy.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:05.600
Then you can take the time and energy you saved, just like concentrating your investment in one stock,

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:11.180
and invest it all in places that are more important to your life, to improve your ability to make money outside of the market,

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.200
and develop your career.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:17.440
This is also a form of concentrated investment, except that your investment target is yourself.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:23.460
So,  concentrated investment and diversified investment,  their strategies do not conflict. If you want to get high returns,

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.620
you are destined to concentrate your investment on one target.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:31.200
Some people meet the conditions for concentrated investment in the stock market, while others meet the conditions for concentrated investment in personal development.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.160
You always need to concentrate your resources in one place and disperse the remaining resources in another.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:41.640
This actually reminds me of Buffett's example. Everyone knows that Buffett,  recommends that ordinary people invest in the S&amp;P 500.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.900
But if you look closely, he is more of a concentrated investor.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:50.640
Most of his capital is placed in a very small number of companies. Is this Buffett,  being hypocritical,

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:51.820
and deceiving us ordinary people?

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:56.920
Not at all. His so-called hypocrisy is precisely his understanding that different people are suitable for different investment strategies.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:05:02.240
It's just like how he responded to a little girl's question at a shareholder meeting a few years ago.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:08.000
The little girl asked him, "It seems like there are no investment opportunities left." He said, "The best thing you can invest in,

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:13.080
is actually yourself." This applies to the little girl, and it also applies to most of us.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.440
What does this have to do with me not looking for the next Tesla?

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:21.400
My investment portfolio has long been Tesla plus the S&amp;P 500. Tesla has already achieved my concentrated investment layout.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.360
I don't go all-in because I want to protect my own margin of safety.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:29.900
So I diversify the rest of my safety margin funds into the S&amp;P 500, so as not to distract my attention,

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:33.340
so that I can focus on my career. I will talk more about this later.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:38.820
For me, looking for the next Tesla is actually taking the middle road,

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.260
which is a half measure.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:46.180
For example, today I invested in,  NVIDIA, tomorrow I invested in AMD,  and then the day after tomorrow I bought Oracle.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:50.920
This seems to have diversified the risk, but in fact my investment portfolio is neither concentrated enough,

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.979
nor truly diversified.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:57.479
For example, if I have a million, and I divide it among seven or eight stocks, how should I allocate it?

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:03.080
Most likely, I will put the vast majority of my funds in Tesla, which I understand best and have the most confidence in, while the positions of other stocks, 

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:08.852
will be very small. In this way, even if I am lucky enough to buy a ten-bagger stock, because the principal is too low,

00:06:08.852 --> 00:06:11.552
it will be insignificant to my overall return.

00:06:11.552 --> 00:06:13.592
More importantly, a person's energy is limited.

00:06:13.592 --> 00:06:18.112
To be honest, just researching Tesla alone has already taken up a lot of my energy.

00:06:18.112 --> 00:06:21.552
 in the past, from Elon Musk's interviews, speeches, and related books,

00:06:21.552 --> 00:06:26.892
to the company's various AI Days, and doing various research, the time consumed is huge.

00:06:26.892 --> 00:06:32.032
At least at this stage, I don't have the energy to study another company in depth.

00:06:32.092 --> 00:06:36.772
Let me give you an example of my own. I once bought some Google stock.

00:06:36.772 --> 00:06:42.032
After ChatGPT came out, I started to feel that Google had a big company disease.

00:06:42.032 --> 00:06:46.432
In the AI era, it might be difficult to turn around. I sold it when I had a slight profit.

00:06:46.432 --> 00:06:52.072
But now that I'm studying AI, I find that my initial judgment of Google on the AI track was inaccurate.

00:06:52.072 --> 00:06:57.352
So you see, my so-called long-term investment in Google was held for a very short time.

00:06:57.352 --> 00:07:02.412
The fundamental reason is that I didn't understand this company enough, or my conviction was not deep enough, so I couldn't hold on to it at all.

00:07:02.472 --> 00:07:05.832
Of course, this doesn't mean you can only go all-in on one stock.

00:07:05.832 --> 00:07:11.812
If you have enough energy to have a deep understanding and conviction in every company in your portfolio, you can of course manage a, 

00:07:11.812 --> 00:07:14.272
concentrated portfolio of multiple stocks.

00:07:14.272 --> 00:07:16.872
But what you will face is,  not only divided energy,

00:07:16.872 --> 00:07:20.892
but also the constant dilemma of how to allocate funds among them.

00:07:20.952 --> 00:07:26.592
To me, this is also doing things halfway, and this half measure will lead to new problems.

00:07:26.592 --> 00:07:31.632
This is the next reason why I don't try to find a second Tesla.

00:07:31.632 --> 00:07:31.902
(Sound effect)

00:07:31.952 --> 00:07:35.031
Chasing hot stocks can easily lead to some bad habits,

00:07:35.032 --> 00:07:39.532
because it will push you into the role of a short-term trader and a gambler.

00:07:39.532 --> 00:07:45.692
This is because when you start asking, "Why didn't I buy that soaring stock?"

00:07:45.692 --> 00:07:49.751
your decision-making starting point has already been hijacked by the stock price performance.

00:07:49.752 --> 00:07:54.312
You start to pay attention to it not because of your conviction after long-term research, but because it has risen.

00:07:54.312 --> 00:07:56.772
This in itself is a very dangerous signal.

00:07:56.892 --> 00:08:02.652
There's a saying I particularly like, I forgot the original words, but it roughly means,  if you are shocked by the world,

00:08:02.652 --> 00:08:05.772
then maybe there is a problem with your cognitive model of the world.

00:08:05.772 --> 00:08:09.092
If you are a true long-term investor and have conviction in a company,

00:08:09.092 --> 00:08:13.691
you should discover its value when its stock price is low or has been performing poorly for a long time,

00:08:13.691 --> 00:08:17.752
not just passively notice it when it soars.

00:08:17.752 --> 00:08:22.252
Being surprised by the surge in stock prices just shows that you haven't done enough homework.

00:08:22.252 --> 00:08:27.252
When you buy because you are chasing the rise, you actually have no conviction in this company, so once it starts to fall,

00:08:27.252 --> 00:08:32.352
you will easily think, ah, maybe I was wrong, maybe this is just a bubble, and then sell it quickly.

00:08:32.352 --> 00:08:37.652
This kind of,  chasing highs and selling lows behavior will make you further and further away from true long-term investing.

00:08:37.732 --> 00:08:43.092
There is a popular joke on the internet that compares short-term trading with long-term holding.  the general idea is that, 

00:08:43.092 --> 00:08:48.351
a person sells a stock every time it rises by 20%. For example, they buy at 20 and sell at 24, buy at 40,

00:08:48.352 --> 00:08:51.032
and sell at 48, making a total of 12.

00:08:51.032 --> 00:08:55.712
But if he had held on from 20 and sold at 48, he would have made 28,

00:08:55.712 --> 00:08:57.112
which is much higher than that 12.

00:08:57.112 --> 00:09:01.572
Compared to long-term investing, short-term trading is more like,  picking up sesame seeds and losing the watermelon.

00:09:01.572 --> 00:09:06.472
Of course, this is a very simplified example, and it ignores complex fluctuations such as declines.

00:09:06.472 --> 00:09:12.432
I recognize that short-term trading has its value, but what I want to emphasize is that it is a completely different game.

00:09:12.432 --> 00:09:15.412
You need to think clearly about what your original intention is.

00:09:15.492 --> 00:09:18.851
If you want to get a tenfold return and find the next Tesla,

00:09:18.852 --> 00:09:21.532
you will most likely need to hold for the long term.

00:09:21.532 --> 00:09:24.532
But the mentality of chasing hotspots will make you FOMO and lose your balance.

00:09:24.532 --> 00:09:29.692
When you catch a soaring stock, you will regret not betting high enough at the time, and your principal is not enough.

00:09:29.692 --> 00:09:30.912
So what to do?

00:09:30.912 --> 00:09:34.192
Many people will choose to add leverage, using margin or options.

00:09:34.192 --> 00:09:37.351
At this time, investing gradually approaches gambling.

00:09:37.352 --> 00:09:42.792
So, I am not willing to look for those so-called next ten-bagger stocks. I don't want them to disrupt my position,

00:09:42.792 --> 00:09:45.392
and turn me into a trader or a gambler.

00:09:45.392 --> 00:09:47.912
My original intention of investing in Tesla was to hold it for the long term.

00:09:47.912 --> 00:09:50.612
In the past, it was my ten-bagger stock, and I believe it will continue to be in the future.

00:09:50.612 --> 00:09:52.732
We will talk more about this at the end.

00:09:54.072 --> 00:09:57.232
There is a saying in English that I particularly like: "What got you here, won't

00:09:57.392 --> 00:09:58.242
get you there."

00:09:58.292 --> 00:10:03.412
The old path that brought you to today will not take you to a new distant place.

00:10:03.412 --> 00:10:07.772
I heard this sentence a long time ago, but a book I've been reading recently

00:10:07.772 --> 00:10:12.172
has given me a deeper understanding of it in terms of personal finance and investment.

00:10:12.172 --> 00:10:14.792
This book is called "The Wealth Ladder."

00:10:14.792 --> 00:10:18.652
I've read "Just Keep Buying" by the same author before.

00:10:18.652 --> 00:10:22.632
And the book we read together in our book club in September is his new book this year.

00:10:22.771 --> 00:10:27.932
In the past few years, my channel has often talked about the topic of financial freedom, but in fact,

00:10:27.932 --> 00:10:32.271
financial freedom is a very subjective and vague concept. It is related to your income, expenses,

00:10:32.271 --> 00:10:34.332
lifestyle, and psychological state.

00:10:34.332 --> 00:10:37.592
And this book, "The Wealth Ladder," directly discards this definition,

00:10:37.592 --> 00:10:41.552
and instead divides wealth into six objective ladders.

00:10:41.612 --> 00:10:45.932
The core idea of this book is that the method you use to get from the first ladder to the second ladder

00:10:45.932 --> 00:10:49.152
may not necessarily help you get from the second ladder to the third ladder.

00:10:49.152 --> 00:10:52.592
If you want to cross different ladders, you need to use different methods.

00:10:52.592 --> 00:10:57.652
For example, I used to say that you should be frugal. When you are initially accumulating capital,

00:10:57.652 --> 00:10:59.512
this is a crucial virtue.

00:10:59.512 --> 00:11:03.872
But when you are already a multi-millionaire, although frugality is still important,

00:11:03.872 --> 00:11:09.192
you can't become a billionaire just by saving money. You need to introduce new methods.

00:11:09.192 --> 00:11:13.031
This is why we cannot blindly imitate the practices of successful people.

00:11:13.032 --> 00:11:19.072
I have previously criticized the kind of investment-linked insurance sold to ordinary people. Many people who refuted me

00:11:19.072 --> 00:11:21.932
would give examples of how much insurance Li Ka-shing bought.

00:11:22.072 --> 00:11:23.832
But Li Ka-shing is Li Ka-shing, and we are not.

00:11:23.832 --> 00:11:27.872
We are at completely different stages of life and capital. He has a family office that we don't have.

00:11:27.872 --> 00:11:33.672
The problems he needs to consider are completely different from ours. Even all our assets are not comparable to the money he pays his lawyers.

00:11:33.672 --> 00:11:38.552
And you simply can't buy the same insurance that Li Ka-shing buys.

00:11:38.552 --> 00:11:41.752
Using his methods to guide our lives is no different from carving a mark on a moving boat to find a sword.

00:11:42.032 --> 00:11:45.192
These are mostly just sales pitches from insurance salespeople.

00:11:45.192 --> 00:11:47.712
You must see clearly which stage you are at.

00:11:47.712 --> 00:11:50.932
So for me, this investment in Tesla has to a large extent, 

00:11:50.932 --> 00:11:54.372
helped me complete a very important leap on the wealth ladder.

00:11:54.372 --> 00:11:57.372
But if I want to go up another level,

00:11:57.372 --> 00:12:02.102
it is very likely that stock investment alone will no longer be able to take me further.

00:12:02.152 --> 00:12:04.332
I shared a statistic in a previous video.

00:12:04.332 --> 00:12:08.032
The truly,  level five and six wealthy people,

00:12:08.032 --> 00:12:13.912
their stock market asset allocation may only account for about 30% of their total assets. This is not intentional on their part,

00:12:13.912 --> 00:12:14.702
to only put in so little.

00:12:14.752 --> 00:12:19.172
The real reason is that the value of their businesses and careers outside the stock market is too high,

00:12:19.172 --> 00:12:23.376
so high that their stock market assets seem small. That is to say,

00:12:23.376 --> 00:12:28.776
what helps them achieve,  the leap across the wealth ladder is their own career.

00:12:28.776 --> 00:12:34.156
This reminds me of a conversation I had many years ago with my friend's father,  who is a successful entrepreneur,

00:12:34.156 --> 00:12:35.436
a billionaire.

00:12:35.496 --> 00:12:39.376
At that time, I asked him, "I have a sum of money. Should I buy a house first,

00:12:39.376 --> 00:12:42.116
or invest it in my own business first?" He asked, "

00:12:42.116 --> 00:12:44.536
what is the return on your business?" I said, "Roughly estimated,

00:12:44.536 --> 00:12:48.096
it's about 1000%." Then he said without hesitation, "Then what are you waiting for?

00:12:48.096 --> 00:12:49.756
Of course you should invest it in your business."

00:12:49.766 --> 00:12:55.236
Looking back at this conversation now, two points have left a deep impression on me. First, I overestimated myself at the time.

00:12:55.236 --> 00:13:01.116
My business could not be scaled simply by investing money, so,  I ended up buying a house.

00:13:01.116 --> 00:13:05.736
However, that experience did teach me a lot of lessons that I can use in my current startup.

00:13:05.836 --> 00:13:09.356
The second interesting point is that when I said a tenfold return,

00:13:09.356 --> 00:13:12.716
that entrepreneur uncle was not surprised at all.

00:13:12.716 --> 00:13:16.876
It was only after many years of starting a business that I understood that for business people, achieving a tenfold,

00:13:16.876 --> 00:13:22.676
or even a hundredfold return is possible and happens from time to time. This is a very important way for individuals to break through the wealth ladder.

00:13:22.756 --> 00:13:25.856
Of course, there is a high risk of failure. Being able to reach level five or six

00:13:25.876 --> 00:13:29.276
is a rare achievement in itself, which speaks for itself.

00:13:29.276 --> 00:13:33.356
But if you want to cross this ladder, investing in your own company,

00:13:33.356 --> 00:13:38.136
the aspects you can manipulate and control are far more than looking for a needle in a haystack in the stock market.

00:13:38.136 --> 00:13:42.036
I have shared this in detail in a previous video, so I won't go into it again.

00:13:42.096 --> 00:13:46.396
So you see, the strategy is phased. In the early stages of the wealth ladder,

00:13:46.396 --> 00:13:50.596
you should focus your energy on your ability to make money outside of the market and invest in yourself.

00:13:50.596 --> 00:13:54.316
In the middle stage, you may indeed need to rely on stock investment.

00:13:54.316 --> 00:13:58.496
And interestingly,  for my current stage, if I want to go up further,

00:13:58.496 --> 00:14:04.236
the next ten-bagger stock I need to invest in may not be another company, but my own business.

00:14:04.236 --> 00:14:08.316
You see, this brings us back to the starting point of investing in yourself.

00:14:08.316 --> 00:14:11.556
So, I highly recommend everyone to read this book.

00:14:12.576 --> 00:14:16.636
The last reason is actually very simple. I believe that Tesla itself still has huge potential.

00:14:16.636 --> 00:14:20.196
There is no need for me to look for a second Tesla.

00:14:20.196 --> 00:14:24.856
After it has risen so much, I am not only continuing to hold it, but I am even constantly buying more.

00:14:24.856 --> 00:14:30.096
The last time I bought was,  after I went to Austin to participate in the Robotaxi,  the first trial operation.

00:14:30.096 --> 00:14:34.976
I believe that Tesla's second wave of growth, a story about physical world AI,

00:14:34.976 --> 00:14:36.616
is just beginning now.

00:14:36.616 --> 00:14:40.936
From FSD V12 to V13, to the introduction of the just-released V14,

00:14:40.936 --> 00:14:45.776
and the rapid development of Optimus in a few years and the third-generation robot waiting in the wings,

00:14:45.776 --> 00:14:48.496
we can already get a glimpse of the future.

00:14:48.636 --> 00:14:54.136
